course: dictionary
lesson: 12982
title: Formal words: expedite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound stiff and grown-up, like the words in a letter from a bank or a school office. Expedite is one of them. Its everyday partners are speed up and hurry along.
explain: Read the clues: «The shop agreed to expedite the delivery, so the parcel arrived two days early.» Arriving two days early means it came faster, so expedite means to make something happen faster.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping in an everyday word: «The shop agreed to speed up the delivery.» The sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Expedite is a verb, so it is something you do: you expedite a delivery, a process or a request. Its other forms are expedites, expedited and expediting, as in «expedited delivery».
fact: Expedite is a verb, and it is formal, so you will mostly meet it in letters, office notices and websites.
fact: «Expedite» means to make something happen faster.
fact: «Expedited delivery» means a parcel or letter is sent faster than usual.
fact: Everyday words with a similar meaning are speed up and hurry along.
fact: The other forms are expedites, expedited and expediting.
exercise: «The office will expedite your application so you get an answer sooner.» What does expedite mean? | *To make something happen faster | To stop something for good | To make something bigger | To write something down carefully
exercise: Which word means the same as expedite? | Stop | *Hurry along | Ignore | Repeat
exercise: The website offers «expedited delivery» for an extra fee. What does expedited suggest? | *Sent faster than usual | Sent much later than usual | Sent in a red box only | Sent back to the shop
test: «The council promised to expedite the repairs after the storm.» What does expedite mean here? | *To speed up the repairs | To paint the repairs | To cancel the repairs | To delay the repairs
test: Which everyday words are the best swap for expedite in «We need to expedite the form»? | Copy it out slowly | *Process it faster | Read it aloud twice | Hide it under the bed
exam: Ella says, «Expedite sounds like a grown-up word, so it must mean slow down.» Is she right? | No, it means to lose something | *No, it means to make something happen faster | Yes, expedite means slow down | Yes, it means to stop completely
